    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-43",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "43 Section 43",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991#sec-43"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "Section 9 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by inserting after subsection (5) the following subsection:\n\"(5A) Where the Director is carrying on a proceeding\ninstituted by another person, being a proceeding of the kind\nmentioned in paragraph (5) (a) or (b), the Director may decline\nto carry it on further even if the Director has not taken it over\nunder subsection (5).\";\n(b) by omitting subsection (6C) and substituting the following\nsubsection:\n\"(6C) In subsection (6B):\n'State or Territory proceedings' means:\n(a) proceedings in a State or Territory:\n(i) for an offence against, or for the recovery of a\npecuniary penalty under, a law of that State or\nTerritory; or\n(ii) in respect of a forfeiture order under a law of that\nState or Territory; or\n(b) proceedings in a State or Territory by way of a coronial\ninquest or inquiry under a law of that State or Territory;\nor\n(c) proceedings in a State or Territory before a prescribed\nauthority or a prescribed body established under a law\nof that State or Territory.\".\nDirector may request assistance of Commissioner of Police",
      "skos:definition": "Section 9 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by inserting after subsection (5) the following subsection:\n\"(5A) Where the Director is carrying on a proceeding\ninstituted by another person, being a proceeding of the kind\nmentioned in paragraph (5) (a) or (b), the Director may decline\nto carry it on further even if the Director has not taken it over\nunder subsection (5).\";\n(b) by omitting subsection (6C) and substituting the following\nsubsection:\n\"(6C) In subsection (6B):\n'State or Territory proceedings' means:\n(a) proceedings in a State or Territory:\n(i) for an offence against, or for the recovery of a\npecuniary penalty under, a law of that State or\nTerritory; or\n(ii) in respect of a forfeiture order under a law of that\nState or Territory; or\n(b) proceedings in a State or Territory by way of a coronial\ninquest or inquiry under a law of that State or Territory;\nor\n(c) proceedings in a State or Territory before a prescribed\nauthority or a prescribed body established under a law\nof that State or Territory.\".\nDirector may request assistance of Commissioner of Police",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-43-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-43-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-43-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "112a2d464518639913260b49ffc9196f8b5960919efa83d0fa9bffb9a9bea6e9",
      "skos:note": "Director may decline to carry on proceeding further"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991#sec-43",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "43 Section 43",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "Section 9 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by inserting after subsection (5) the following subsection:\n\"(5A) Where the Director is carrying on a proceeding\ninstituted by another person, being a proceeding of the kind\nmentioned in paragraph (5) (a) or (b), the Director may decline\nto carry it on further even if the Director has not taken it over\nunder subsection (5).\";\n(b) by omitting subsection (6C) and substituting the following\nsubsection:\n\"(6C) In subsection (6B):\n'State or Territory proceedings' means:\n(a) proceedings in a State or Territory:\n(i) for an offence against, or for the recovery of a\npecuniary penalty under, a law of that State or\nTerritory; or\n(ii) in respect of a forfeiture order under a law of that\nState or Territory; or\n(b) proceedings in a State or Territory by way of a coronial\ninquest or inquiry under a law of that State or Territory;\nor\n(c) proceedings in a State or Territory before a prescribed\nauthority or a prescribed body established under a law\nof that State or Territory.\".\nDirector may request assistance of Commissioner of Police"
    },
