    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-45",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45 After section 18 of the Principal Act the following sections are",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991#sec-45"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "inserted:\nAppointment etc. of Associate Director\n\"18A. (1) The Associate Director must be appointed by the\nGovernor-General.\n\"(2) The Associate Director holds office for the period, not longer\nthan 7 years, specified in the instrument of appointment, but is eligible\nfor re-appointment.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment\nNo. 28, 1991\n\"(3) A person must not be appointed as the Associate Director\nunless he or she is a legal practitioner and has been a legal practitioner\nfor at least 5 years.\n\"(4) A person who has turned 65 must not be appointed as the\nAssociate Director and a person must not be appointed for a period\nthat ends after the day on which the person will turn 65.\n\"(5) The Associate Director holds office on such terms and\nconditions (if any) in respect of matters not provided for by this Act\nas are determined by the Governor-General.\nExercise of powers and functions by Associate Director\n\"18B. (1) Subject to any directions of the Director, the Associate\nDirector has all the powers and functions of the Director, except the\nDirector's powers of delegation under section 31.\n\"(2) A power or function that is exercised or performed by the\nAssociate Director is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been\nexercised or performed by the Director.\n\"(3) Where, under this Act, the exercise of a power or performance\nof a function by the Director depends on the opinion, belief or state of\nmind of the Director in relation to a matter, the power or function\nmay be exercised or performed by the Associate Director depending on\nthe opinion, belief or state of mind of the Associate Director in relation\nto that matter.\".\nRemuneration and allowances",
      "skos:definition": "inserted:\nAppointment etc. of Associate Director\n\"18A. (1) The Associate Director must be appointed by the\nGovernor-General.\n\"(2) The Associate Director holds office for the period, not longer\nthan 7 years, specified in the instrument of appointment, but is eligible\nfor re-appointment.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment\nNo. 28, 1991\n\"(3) A person must not be appointed as the Associate Director\nunless he or she is a legal practitioner and has been a legal practitioner\nfor at least 5 years.\n\"(4) A person who has turned 65 must not be appointed as the\nAssociate Director and a person must not be appointed for a period\nthat ends after the day on which the person will turn 65.\n\"(5) The Associate Director holds office on such terms and\nconditions (if any) in respect of matters not provided for by this Act\nas are determined by the Governor-General.\nExercise of powers and functions by Associate Director\n\"18B. (1) Subject to any directions of the Director, the Associate\nDirector has all the powers and functions of the Director, except the\nDirector's powers of delegation under section 31.\n\"(2) A power or function that is exercised or performed by the\nAssociate Director is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been\nexercised or performed by the Director.\n\"(3) Where, under this Act, the exercise of a power or performance\nof a function by the Director depends on the opinion, belief or state of\nmind of the Director in relation to a matter, the power or function\nmay be exercised or performed by the Associate Director depending on\nthe opinion, belief or state of mind of the Associate Director in relation\nto that matter.\".\nRemuneration and allowances",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-45-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-45-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2f8a022dce9955e5da057323733ce6b71f18278f75f9f62161c844b14105473f",
      "skos:note": "Appointment requirements for Associate Director"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991#sec-45",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45 After section 18 of the Principal Act the following sections are",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "inserted:\nAppointment etc. of Associate Director\n\"18A. (1) The Associate Director must be appointed by the\nGovernor-General.\n\"(2) The Associate Director holds office for the period, not longer\nthan 7 years, specified in the instrument of appointment, but is eligible\nfor re-appointment.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment\nNo. 28, 1991\n\"(3) A person must not be appointed as the Associate Director\nunless he or she is a legal practitioner and has been a legal practitioner\nfor at least 5 years.\n\"(4) A person who has turned 65 must not be appointed as the\nAssociate Director and a person must not be appointed for a period\nthat ends after the day on which the person will turn 65.\n\"(5) The Associate Director holds office on such terms and\nconditions (if any) in respect of matters not provided for by this Act\nas are determined by the Governor-General.\nExercise of powers and functions by Associate Director\n\"18B. (1) Subject to any directions of the Director, the Associate\nDirector has all the powers and functions of the Director, except the\nDirector's powers of delegation under section 31.\n\"(2) A power or function that is exercised or performed by the\nAssociate Director is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been\nexercised or performed by the Director.\n\"(3) Where, under this Act, the exercise of a power or performance\nof a function by the Director depends on the opinion, belief or state of\nmind of the Director in relation to a matter, the power or function\nmay be exercised or performed by the Associate Director depending on\nthe opinion, belief or state of mind of the Associate Director in relation\nto that matter.\".\nRemuneration and allowances"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-45-norm",
