      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "Section 24 of the Principal Act is amended by adding at the\nend the following subsection:\n\"(2) The Associate Director musjt give written notice to the AttorneyGeneral of all direct and indirect pecuniary interests that the Associate\nDirector has or acquires in any business, whether in Australia or\nanywhere else, or in any body corporate carrying on any such business.\".\nOath or affirmation of office",
      "skos:definition": "Section 24 of the Principal Act is amended by adding at the\nend the following subsection:\n\"(2) The Associate Director musjt give written notice to the AttorneyGeneral of all direct and indirect pecuniary interests that the Associate\nDirector has or acquires in any business, whether in Australia or\nanywhere else, or in any body corporate carrying on any such business.\".\nOath or affirmation of office",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-51-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-51-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0afaf2f610e91c3cff3c6bd6f78683e3270fb1456b7fd492d3c11f11ea253a18",
      "skos:note": "Associate Director must give written notice of pecuniary interests to AttorneyGeneral",
      "dc:description": "written notice"
    },
