    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-55",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55 Section 55",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991#sec-55"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "Section 27 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting subsection (2) and substituting the following\nsubsection:\n\"(2) The Director has all the powers of, or exercisable by, a\nSecretary under the Public Service Act 1922 so far as those\npowers relate to the branch of the Australian Public Service\ncomprising the staff mentioned in subsection (1) as if that\nbranch were a separate Department of the Service.\";\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment\nNo. 28, 1991\n(b) by omitting from subsection (3) \"and with the approval of the\nAttorney-General or a person authorised in writing by the\nAttorney-General to grant approvals under this subsection\";\n(c) by omitting from subsection (4) \"subsection (1)\" and substituting\n\"subsection (3)\";\n(d) by omitting from subsection (4) \", with the approval of the\nPublic Service Board\".\nDelegation by Director",
      "skos:definition": "Section 27 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting subsection (2) and substituting the following\nsubsection:\n\"(2) The Director has all the powers of, or exercisable by, a\nSecretary under the Public Service Act 1922 so far as those\npowers relate to the branch of the Australian Public Service\ncomprising the staff mentioned in subsection (1) as if that\nbranch were a separate Department of the Service.\";\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment\nNo. 28, 1991\n(b) by omitting from subsection (3) \"and with the approval of the\nAttorney-General or a person authorised in writing by the\nAttorney-General to grant approvals under this subsection\";\n(c) by omitting from subsection (4) \"subsection (1)\" and substituting\n\"subsection (3)\";\n(d) by omitting from subsection (4) \", with the approval of the\nPublic Service Board\".\nDelegation by Director",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-55-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-55-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-55-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9d47886618205928c01da7a38594dede6f4d390baa761c0eafaf59034518b34c",
      "skos:note": "Amends Section 27 of the Principal Act regarding Director's powers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991#sec-55",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55 Section 55",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "Section 27 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting subsection (2) and substituting the following\nsubsection:\n\"(2) The Director has all the powers of, or exercisable by, a\nSecretary under the Public Service Act 1922 so far as those\npowers relate to the branch of the Australian Public Service\ncomprising the staff mentioned in subsection (1) as if that\nbranch were a separate Department of the Service.\";\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment\nNo. 28, 1991\n(b) by omitting from subsection (3) \"and with the approval of the\nAttorney-General or a person authorised in writing by the\nAttorney-General to grant approvals under this subsection\";\n(c) by omitting from subsection (4) \"subsection (1)\" and substituting\n\"subsection (3)\";\n(d) by omitting from subsection (4) \", with the approval of the\nPublic Service Board\".\nDelegation by Director"
    },
