    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-73",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "73 Section 73",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991#sec-73"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The section 34 declaration in force immediately before the\ncommencing day continues to have effect on and after that day as if:\n(a) it had been made under section 34 of the Principal Act, as\namended by this Act; and\n(b) it declared the New South Wales Crime Commission to be an\nagency for the purposes of the Principal Act as so amended.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment\nNo. 28, 1991\n(2) Any warrant or other document given or issued under the\nPrincipal Act, and in force immediately before the commencing day,\ncontinues to have effect on and after that day as if it had been given\nor issued under the Principal Act, as amended by this Act, and for that\npurpose:\n(a) references in the warrant or document to the State Drug Crime\nCommission of New South Wales are taken to be references to\nthe New South Wales Crime Commission; and\n(b) references in the warrant or document to the chief officer or\nChairperson of the State Drug Crime Commission of New\nSouth Wales are taken to be references to the chief officer or\nChairperson of the New South Wales Crime Commission; and\n(c) references in the warrant or document to a member, or member\nof the staff, of the State Drug Crime Commission of New South\nWales are taken to be references to a member, or member of\nthe staff, of the New South Wales Crime Commission.\n(3) This section does not prevent the Minister from revoking under\nsection 37 of the Principal Act, as amended by this Act, a declaration\nto which subsection (1) of this section applies.\n(4) In this section:\n\"commencing day\" means the day on which subsection 61 (2) of this\nAct commences;\n\"section 34 declaration\" means a declaration made under section 34 of\nthe Principal Act declaring the State Drug Crime Commission of New\nSouth Wales to be an agency for the purposes of that Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The section 34 declaration in force immediately before the\ncommencing day continues to have effect on and after that day as if:\n(a) it had been made under section 34 of the Principal Act, as\namended by this Act; and\n(b) it declared the New South Wales Crime Commission to be an\nagency for the purposes of the Principal Act as so amended.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment\nNo. 28, 1991\n(2) Any warrant or other document given or issued under the\nPrincipal Act, and in force immediately before the commencing day,\ncontinues to have effect on and after that day as if it had been given\nor issued under the Principal Act, as amended by this Act, and for that\npurpose:\n(a) references in the warrant or document to the State Drug Crime\nCommission of New South Wales are taken to be references to\nthe New South Wales Crime Commission; and\n(b) references in the warrant or document to the chief officer or\nChairperson of the State Drug Crime Commission of New\nSouth Wales are taken to be references to the chief officer or\nChairperson of the New South Wales Crime Commission; and\n(c) references in the warrant or document to a member, or member\nof the staff, of the State Drug Crime Commission of New South\nWales are taken to be references to a member, or member of\nthe staff, of the New South Wales Crime Commission.\n(3) This section does not prevent the Minister from revoking under\nsection 37 of the Principal Act, as amended by this Act, a declaration\nto which subsection (1) of this section applies.\n(4) In this section:\n\"commencing day\" means the day on which subsection 61 (2) of this\nAct commences;\n\"section 34 declaration\" means a declaration made under section 34 of\nthe Principal Act declaring the State Drug Crime Commission of New\nSouth Wales to be an agency for the purposes of that Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-73-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-73-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-73-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-73-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "28f5b2c1d5cf871fa78419d857c20f66d6a4b1b794477a6564303d80abd03702"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991#sec-73",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "73 Section 73",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The section 34 declaration in force immediately before the\ncommencing day continues to have effect on and after that day as if:\n(a) it had been made under section 34 of the Principal Act, as\namended by this Act; and\n(b) it declared the New South Wales Crime Commission to be an\nagency for the purposes of the Principal Act as so amended.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment\nNo. 28, 1991\n(2) Any warrant or other document given or issued under the\nPrincipal Act, and in force immediately before the commencing day,\ncontinues to have effect on and after that day as if it had been given\nor issued under the Principal Act, as amended by this Act, and for that\npurpose:\n(a) references in the warrant or document to the State Drug Crime\nCommission of New South Wales are taken to be references to\nthe New South Wales Crime Commission; and\n(b) references in the warrant or document to the chief officer or\nChairperson of the State Drug Crime Commission of New\nSouth Wales are taken to be references to the chief officer or\nChairperson of the New South Wales Crime Commission; and\n(c) references in the warrant or document to a member, or member\nof the staff, of the State Drug Crime Commission of New South\nWales are taken to be references to a member, or member of\nthe staff, of the New South Wales Crime Commission.\n(3) This section does not prevent the Minister from revoking under\nsection 37 of the Principal Act, as amended by this Act, a declaration\nto which subsection (1) of this section applies.\n(4) In this section:\n\"commencing day\" means the day on which subsection 61 (2) of this\nAct commences;\n\"section 34 declaration\" means a declaration made under section 34 of\nthe Principal Act declaring the State Drug Crime Commission of New\nSouth Wales to be an agency for the purposes of that Act."
    },
